<title>Core Concepts</title>
<description>The mental model for how MemeWarzone works.</description>
<content>If you understand these concepts, everything else in MemeWarzone becomes easy. ## The 60-second overview 1. A **Creator** launches a **Campaign** (a token) in seconds. 2. Traders buy/sell on a **bonding curve**. 3. As the curve fills, the campaign approaches **Graduation**. 4. Discovery is driven by **UpVotes** and competitive **Leagues**. 5. Fees fund **creator earnings**, **league prize pools**, and **protocol operations**. ## Concepts (recommended reading order) - **[Campaigns](/core-concepts/campaigns)** — what you’re trading and what “launching” means. - **[Bonding Curve](/core-concepts/bonding-curve)** — why the price changes as people trade. - **[Graduation](/core-concepts/graduation)** — what happens when a campaign “makes it.” - **[UpVotes](/core-concepts/upvotes)** — paid discovery that moves visibility. - **[Leagues](/core-concepts/leagues)** — weekly/monthly competitions funded by activity. - **[Fees & Treasury](/core-concepts/fees-and-treasury)** — where the money goes (plain English). - **[Claims](/core-concepts/claims)** — how eligible wallets collect rewards. If you’re here to trade, jump next to **For Traders → Trading basics**.</content>
