<title>League Categories</title>
<description>The five main MemeWarzone League categories and what each one rewards.</description>
<content>MemeWarzone has five core League categories. Each category rewards a different type of battlefield performance. ## Perfect Run Perfect Run rewards campaigns that achieve a clean run based on strict campaign behavior rules. Direction: - monthly-only category - jackpot-style potential - rollover if no campaign qualifies - designed to reward rare, clean launch execution ## Fastest Finish Fastest Finish rewards campaigns that graduate the fastest. Important rule direction: - creator buys should be excluded from the measurement - the category should focus on real external campaign demand ## Biggest Hit Biggest Hit rewards the biggest single buy during the bonding-curve phase. This category creates dramatic moments around major entries. ## Top Earner Top Earner rewards the strongest trader performance. The intent is to track meaningful trader earnings within the defined League rules and epoch. ## Crowd Favorite Crowd Favorite rewards campaigns that win the attention battle through UpVotes. This is the most community-driven category. ## Why multiple categories matter A single leaderboard usually favors whales. Multiple categories create more ways to win: - clean launch execution - speed - conviction - trading skill - community support This makes the warzone more dynamic than a simple volume leaderboard.</content>
