<loc>https://docs.memewar.zone/treasury/weekly-distribution</loc>
<title>Weekly Distribution</title>
<description>The weekly treasury policy for operations, retention, and founder payouts.</description>
<content>MemeWarzone treasury movement should follow a fixed weekly order. The point is to remove emotional decision-making from money flow. ## Weekly cadence Choose a fixed weekly moment, such as Monday. Every week, execute the same order. ## Step 1 — Ops normalization Bring the Ops Safe back to its target balance. Target: **50 BNB**. - If Ops Safe is below 50 BNB, top it up. - If Ops Safe is above 50 BNB, sweep excess back to Owners Safe. ## Step 2 — Treasury retention A fixed percentage stays in the Owners Safe. This funds: - audits - emergencies - legal - growth - partnerships - infrastructure buffers ## Step 3 — Founder payouts The remaining configured percentage is paid to predefined founder payout wallets according to the agreed split. This happens on schedule without renegotiating every week. ## What this prevents The weekly policy helps prevent: - one person secretly taking fees - one person blocking normal payout flow indefinitely - operational funds becoming too large - protocol revenue landing in developer wallets - weekly financial arguments ## Non-goal MemeWarzone should not auto-split protocol fees on-chain directly to personal wallets. Policy-driven treasury distribution is more flexible and safer long term.</content>
</page>
<page>
<loc>https://docs.memewar.zone/treasury/where-does-revenue-go</loc>
<title>Where does revenue go?</title>
<description>Plain-English revenue flow from protocol → treasury → payouts.</description>
<content>## Step 1 — Revenue goes to Owners Safe Owners Safe is a **2-of-3 multisig** treasury wallet. No personal wallets receive protocol fees directly. ## Step 2 — Ops Safe stays at 50 BNB Ops Safe is capped runway for operations: - if below 50 → top up - if above 50 → sweep excess back ## Step 3 — Weekly distribution On a fixed weekly cadence: 1) normalize Ops Safe to 50 2) retain treasury buffer % 3) distribute remaining % to founder payout wallets We avoid on-chain auto-splitting to individuals for safety and flexibility.</content>
