<page>
<loc>https://docs.memewar.zone/what-is-memewarzone</loc>
<title>What is MemeWarzone?</title>
<description/>
<content># What is MemeWarzone? MemeWarzone is a competitive on-chain ecosystem where every meme token campaign becomes part of a recurring arena. Think of it as: - **Campaign system**: creators prepare and launch public meme campaigns - **Market**: traders buy and sell through a bonding curve before graduation - **Discovery layer**: UpVotes push campaigns into visible competition - **Competition layer**: Leagues run on epochs and distribute prizes - **Incentive layer**: recruiters, squads, and Warzone BNB Airdrops turn activity into rewards - **Progression layer**: ranks, profiles, and leaderboards make participation visible ## The campaign lifecycle 1. **Create**: a creator launches a campaign with token and bonding curve. 2. **Trade**: users buy and sell against the curve. 3. **UpVote**: the community boosts visibility for campaigns they support. 4. **Graduate**: the campaign reaches 50 BNB, finalizes, and creates liquidity. 5. **Compete**: campaigns, traders, recruiters, and squads participate in epochs, rankings, and rewards. 6. **Claim**: eligible users claim rewards through official dashboard/profile flows. If you are looking for specifics: - full flow: **[How MemeWarzone Works](/how-memewarzone-works)** - lifecycle mechanics: **[Campaign System](/platform/campaign-lifecycle)** - pricing: **[Bonding Curve](/platform/bonding-curve)** - post-threshold transition: **[Graduation](/platform/graduation)**</content>
</page>
<page>
<loc>https://docs.memewar.zone/why-we-built-this</loc>
<title>Why we built this</title>
<description/>
<content># Why we built MemeWarzone Many meme campaign markets optimize for platform extraction: - creators pay to launch, pay to promote, and still get buried - traders get short-term hype cycles and no long-term game loop - platforms take fees, but value does not flow back to the people who make the ecosystem valuable We built MemeWarzone around a simple idea: > Creators, traders, recruiters, and communities should be part of the system's upside. ## 1. Fix discovery Discovery often turns into pay-to-play shilling. MemeWarzone replaces hidden boosts with UpVotes, a clear way to show support and push campaigns up the rankings. ## 2. Make campaigns worth returning to Leagues turn trading and creator performance into weekly and monthly competition. Winners get rewarded. Campaigns get spotlighted. The ecosystem stays alive. ## 3. Add progression and growth systems Profiles, rankings, recruiters, squads, and public leaderboards give users a reason to keep building. Users are not just anonymous flow. They can build status and compound their presence inside the ecosystem. ## 4. Keep money flow transparent TreasuryRouter routes fees into reward buckets and protocol revenue. The treasury model then separates protocol revenue, Owners Safe policy, and Ops Safe execution. If you want the mechanics, start with: - **[How MemeWarzone Works](/how-memewarzone-works)** - **[Fee Routing](/fees/fee-routing)** - **[Treasury Structure](/treasury)**</content>
</page>
